<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Android 12+ launch screen.

    From API 31 the platform draws the launch screen itself and IGNORES
    android:windowBackground for it, so drawable/launch_background.xml — which
    is still correct, and still used on older devices — has no effect here.

    With no icon supplied, the system falls back to the launcher icon. Ours is
    a legacy (non-adaptive) bitmap of a black rounded square, and the platform
    centres a legacy icon inside its own white rounded container. That is the
    two nested boxes on the launch screen: the white one belongs to Android,
    the black one is ic_launcher itself. Neither is anything this app asked
    for.

    Naming a transparent-background icon removes both. windowSplashScreenIcon-
    BackgroundColor is deliberately NOT set: setting it would reinstate a
    circle behind the mark, which is the thing being removed.

    The icon is generated by ziren_dashboard/scripts/make-splash-icon.mjs,
    which also handles the sizing rule — the platform masks the icon to a
    circle and only guarantees the inner two thirds, so the mark is padded to
    sit inside that.

    Since 2026-10-02 the icon is splash_blank (nothing): the Flutter splash
    plays the logo drawing itself in, and a finished mark shown first would
    vanish and draw again. The launch screen is the plain background.
-->
<resources>
    <style name="LaunchTheme" parent="@android:style/Theme.Light.NoTitleBar">
        <item name="android:windowSplashScreenBackground">@color/zirenBackground</item>
        <item name="android:windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon">@drawable/splash_blank</item>
        <!-- Kept for the window itself once the splash hands over. -->
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@color/zirenBackground</item>
        <item name="android:windowFullscreen">true</item>
    </style>

    <style name="NormalTheme" parent="@android:style/Theme.Light.NoTitleBar">
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@color/zirenBackground</item>
    </style>
</resources>
